      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T13:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nothing on the QUIC path sends packets while a non-SSE request is still being processed, so any HTTP/3 request taking over 30 s (e.g. a mounted-device RPC, whose default timeout is 60 s) now has its connection silently dropped with no response. Could we either raise this default above the longest server-side request timeout, or at least document in this description and the user guide that the timeout must exceed it?",
